  "scope": [
    "Two distinct same-owner alternate archives are retained in native owner and digest order. A valid target carrying the newer alternate in place of the earlier archive is refused before the epoch advances; the target carrying both originals passes.",
    "Following an actual restart, source and independent SDKs reopen each alternate separately and exercise document and comment Undo/Redo. Neither alternate is submitted as live work during the handover.",
    "After the first authenticated replacement accepts additional document and review events, a second live commit rejects an otherwise verified target missing the retained alternate and leaves the first epoch current.",
    "The second approved target retains the same exact alternate, the advanced accepted cut, and the recaptured selected participant. After moving the earlier room and original files aside, the independent SDKs recover both views, check future document and review Undo/Redo and deliver the four pending selected outbox entries.",
    "An authenticated owner exports the exact retained binary from the live resumed relay. Wrong authentication, stale epoch and occupied export destination refuse. The independent SDK verifies the exact exported pin and binary against the retained alternate.",
    "A native authenticated handover binds the selected journal cohort and the exact alternate participant file into the replacement epoch. The alternate remains separate from live provider inputs and delivery.",
    "An independent cold reopen refuses changed alternate bytes. A matching replacement resumes its original pending deliveries and retains the competing archive after the original source directories are moved.",
    "Both source and offline-installed SDK consumers recover the retained alternate in independent client storage, compare the complete original recovery state, and exercise document and comment Undo and Redo with transport disconnected."
